DECWIN-WORDSTORE: the decompress window @0x789354 is a 16-bit field

dec_info+0xc is TWO 16-bit fields: window size @0x789354 and the new-stream flag
@0x789356 (Decompress parses the per-block stream header only when the flag is set,
resetting dest/remaining). The original writes the window with `mov WORD PTR
ds:0x789354` (asm @0x4309f3/0x430a51...), but _DAT_00789354 is int-typed so Ghidra's
`_DAT_00789354 = 0x4000;` became a 32-bit store ZEROING the flag -> Decompress treated
every flushed block as a continuation of the previous stream (stale remaining=0x263200,
dest marching on) -> streamed straight over the block end into the adjacent OT
(the DrawOTag 0x24af corruption; watchpoint-proven). Reads/writes that genuinely span
both fields (`_DAT_00789354 >> 0x10`, `CONCAT22(_DAT_00789356,0x4000)`) stay 32-bit.
Reference layout comparison (live dd2h.exe under Wine) confirmed our allocation history
matches the original (L9 OT=0x3200 entries explains the layout difference vs L1) --
the corruption was purely this flag clobber. All six window stores patched to word width.

